## [06/05/2026 23:45] - US-011
- What was implemented: Karaoke-style synchronized lyrics highlighting — LRC timestamp parsing into timed lines, auto-scroll to current verse, and distinct visual highlighting
- Files changed: android/app/src/main/java/com/mediacontrol/app/ui/LyricsScreen.kt, android/AGENTS.md, prd.json, progress.txt
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Patterns discovered: `LyricsLine` data class carries `timeMs: Long` and `text: String` for timed LRC lines
  - Patterns discovered: Regex `\[(\d{2}):(\d{2})\.?(\d*)\]` captures minutes, seconds, and fractional seconds; handle 2-digit (centiseconds *10) and 3-digit (milliseconds) precision
  - Patterns discovered: Karaoke highlighting uses `findCurrentLineIndex()` with `LazyListState.animateScrollToItem()` keyed on `currentLineIndex` for smooth auto-scroll
  - Gotchas encountered: `animateScrollToItem` called in `LaunchedEffect` — key on `currentLineIndex` so it only fires when the target line changes, not every frame
  - Gotchas encountered: Lines without timestamps (timeMs=0) are skipped in current line matching to avoid false positives
  - Useful context: `itemsIndexed` from `androidx.compose.foundation.lazy.itemsIndexed` is needed for indexed rendering in LazyColumn
  - Useful context: `rememberLazyListState()` provides stable list state for scroll control across recompositions
